    "issue_key": "MER-117",
    "summary": "Invoice line versions advance before the event is durable",
    "description": "A retry after a broker interruption is rejected as stale even though downstream consumers never received the prior line-item update.\n\nTribal constraint: The outbox consumer is writer of record; version advancement happens only after durable publish/consumer application, not when the HTTP producer assembles the event.",
